1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:06,996
Copilot opens pull requests far faster than teams can
verify them, and they reach production unverified.

2
00:00:06,996 --> 00:00:12,175
We built The Last Human to get from agentic coding to
trusted agentic coding.

3
00:00:12,175 --> 00:00:16,002
Agentic AI rests on one premise above all others.

4
00:00:16,002 --> 00:00:18,206
AI has to stay under human control.

5
00:00:18,206 --> 00:00:21,092
Without that, we lose permission to operate at all.

6
00:00:21,092 --> 00:00:24,910
And the method proposed is observability at every
layer.

7
00:00:24,910 --> 00:00:28,399
Agents are already in every stage of the SDLC.

8
00:00:28,399 --> 00:00:30,529
Copilot writes the implementation,

9
00:00:30,529 --> 00:00:33,322
tests and review run automatically,

10
00:00:33,322 --> 00:00:35,680
deploy and operate leave records too.

11
00:00:35,680 --> 00:00:37,527
Merge alone records nothing.

12
00:00:37,527 --> 00:00:38,733
The load lands here.

13
00:00:38,733 --> 00:00:44,278
This judgment has been left to intuition. Everyone
predicted AI would make them faster.

14
00:00:44,278 --> 00:00:49,186
Measured, they were nineteen percent slower.
Self-report is not evidence.

15
00:00:49,186 --> 00:00:52,486
The gaps in agentic coding are already being measured.

16
00:00:52,486 --> 00:00:58,198
A paper this year analyzed twenty-three thousand
agentic pull requests.

17
00:00:58,198 --> 00:01:04,294
Descriptions often did not match the code, and
twenty-eight percent of those PRs were approved

18
00:01:04,294 --> 00:01:04,748
anyway.

19
00:01:04,748 --> 00:01:08,098
The authors call for a mechanism to verify this.

20
00:01:08,098 --> 00:01:10,910
We took that as our starting point and built one.

21
00:01:10,910 --> 00:01:14,847
Parts of the industry answered by banning AI
contributions.

22
00:01:14,847 --> 00:01:18,584
Simple, but it gives up the productivity along with
the risk.

23
00:01:18,584 --> 00:01:24,059
Instead of banning, we verify only the risky changes
and keep the understanding.

24
00:01:24,059 --> 00:01:26,846
So we reversed the direction of explanation.

25
00:01:26,846 --> 00:01:29,008
Other tools have the model explain.

26
00:01:29,008 --> 00:01:31,158
Here the person answers the model.

27
00:01:31,158 --> 00:01:33,695
And that answer binds to the commit.

28
00:01:33,695 --> 00:01:35,120
Let me show you it working.

29
00:03:03,120 --> 00:03:06,132
We put this gate on our own pull requests first.

30
00:03:06,132 --> 00:03:09,457
It fired on twenty-six, and fifteen of them stopped.

31
00:03:09,457 --> 00:03:12,232
Every file carrying judgment stopped us.

32
00:03:12,232 --> 00:03:15,894
Deleting authentication code stays under the
threshold.

33
00:03:15,894 --> 00:03:19,406
And twelve merged while pending. We report that too.

34
00:03:19,406 --> 00:03:22,213
This is the path one pull request travels.

35
00:03:22,213 --> 00:03:24,972
Actions recomputes the risk itself.

36
00:03:24,972 --> 00:03:28,114
Below the threshold it merges with no check.

37
00:03:28,114 --> 00:03:30,607
Above it, the author answers from the code.

38
00:03:30,607 --> 00:03:32,689
The receipt binds to the commit.

39
00:03:32,689 --> 00:03:34,628
Only a match opens the gate.

40
00:03:34,628 --> 00:03:37,080
The server's word alone is not enough.

41
00:03:37,080 --> 00:03:39,389
Adoption runs on three tracks.

42
00:03:39,389 --> 00:03:41,912
An operator stands up the server once,

43
00:03:41,912 --> 00:03:45,314
three files per repository, required check last.

44
00:03:45,314 --> 00:03:47,646
The author answers two questions.

45
00:03:47,646 --> 00:03:49,581
There are no long-lived secrets.

46
00:03:49,581 --> 00:03:53,043
AI cannot take responsibility, but a person can.

47
00:03:53,043 --> 00:03:55,830
For that, understanding has to be on record.

48
00:03:55,830 --> 00:03:59,617
Not slowing down, but raising the speed we can carry.

49
00:03:59,617 --> 00:04:02,292
It is running on this repository right now.

50
00:04:02,292 --> 00:04:05,704
AI-generated code. Human-owned decisions.
